{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux relies on specific patterns to ensure correct "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" behavior, efficient rendering, and safe concurrency. This article explains the reasoning behind these patterns."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"The Snapshot Pattern","anchor":"The-Snapshot-Pattern","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Store.send()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" copies the observer tree into a local struct, mutates the copy via the reducer, then assigns changed properties back. This happens internally via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State(observer:)"},{"text":" packs, ","type":"text"},{"code":"State.apply(_:to:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" unpacks.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The pattern exists for two reasons:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" equality checking."}]},{"text":" The ","type":"text"},{"code":"set","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" accessor checks ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and suppresses no-op notifications. Swift’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"_modify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" accessor (used by ","type":"text"},{"code":"inout","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") fires notifications unconditionally. The snapshot pattern routes through ","type":"text"},{"code":"set","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Cross-slice observation isolation.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" macro generates a separate "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" class for each ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"text":" property. A view reading ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.items"},{"text":" won’t re-render when only ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.ui"},{"text":" changes, because they live on different observer objects.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" macro generates the observer class tree and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance automatically. Hand-written conformance is still possible for advanced cases — see "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxObservable","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Explicit equality guards ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"if x != state.x { x = state.x }"},{"type":"text","text":") are unnecessary. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" already checks equality on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"type":"text","text":". Unconditional assignment is safe."}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Note"},{"anchor":"Dispatch-Loop-Detection","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Dispatch Loop Detection"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" warns if "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" is called more than 100 times per debounce interval. This usually means "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send()"},{"type":"text","text":" isn’t using the snapshot pattern, causing cascading re-renders that trigger re-dispatches."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Reducer Weight","anchor":"Reducer-Weight"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers run synchronously on the MainActor. Move O(n²) work into an "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect"},{"type":"text","text":" and dispatch the result back as an action."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Effect Threading","anchor":"Effect-Threading","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"name":"Important","style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effects run on Swift concurrency’s cooperative thread pool via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task { @concurrent in }"},{"type":"text","text":". Blocking calls ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Process.waitUntilExit()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DispatchSemaphore.wait()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Thread.sleep()"},{"type":"text","text":") hold threads hostage. If enough block, the pool starves and the MainActor freezes."}]}],"type":"aside"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use async alternatives: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"terminationHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" + continuation instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"waitUntilExit()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task.sleep()"},{"type":"text","text":" instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Thread.sleep()"},{"type":"text","text":", async file I\/O instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data(contentsOf:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Architecture & Performance"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide"]}],"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"],"title":"Explanation","generated":true}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxObservable":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SwiduxObservable","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxObservable","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxObservable"}],"title":"SwiduxObservable","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxobservable","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Bridges a value-type state struct to an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" class tree for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"per-property SwiftUI observation granularity.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","title":"Effect","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}],"abstract":[{"text":"An async unit of work returned by a reducer.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","title":"Plugin Architecture","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/DesignPrinciples":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples","title":"Design Principles","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","abstract":[{"text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them.","type":"text"}],"role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","title":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"title":"Swidux","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","role":"collection"}}}